# Attendî — frontend environment
#
# Copy to `.env` for local development:
#     copy .env.example .env
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL is the axios base path. The value below is a RELATIVE path
# ("/api/v1") on purpose: vite.config.js proxies /api -> http://localhost:8000,
# so the browser only ever talks to its own origin (localhost:5173). That keeps
# the Django session cookie same-origin, so SameSite=Lax works over plain HTTP
# in development. There is deliberately NO hardcoded localhost:8000 fallback in
# src/api/client.js — a missing .env fails loudly instead of silently switching
# to an untested cross-origin path.
#
# At deploy time, if the API lives on a different domain, this becomes an
# absolute https:// URL AND the backend must set SESSION_COOKIE_SAMESITE=None
# with SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE=True and CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS to include the
# frontend origin.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1
